{
  "description": "Scripts and what the fake receiver must do with them, the same in Go and Python (T-04.8). config: expected_bearer, expected_api_key {header,value}, default_status. script: the answers in order; an answer is {status, retry_after?, location?, delay_ms?} or {close: true} or {truncate: true}. requests: what the test sends (body text, gzip? to compress it, headers?). expected: per request the status (or connection_error / body_error), headers the answer must carry, a text its body must contain, a minimum elapsed time. expected_recorded: how many requests were recorded, how many events in the valid batches, the invalid reasons (each a text the recorded reason must contain, in order) and how many requests were gzipped. A request that the fake rejects (400 invalid body, 401 authentication) is still recorded.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "description": "With an empty script the fake answers 200 to a valid batch and records the batch, its headers and its events.",
      "config": {},
      "script": [],
      "requests": [
        {
          "body": "{\"events\":[{\"data\":{\"category\":\"http\",\"message\":\"one\"},\"event_id\":\"01900000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001\",\"event_type\":\"log.entry.recorded\",\"occurred_at\":\"2026-10-28T10:00:00.123456Z\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-10-28T10:00:00.123456Z\",\"resource\":{\"instance_id\":\"hub-01\",\"service_name\":\"sensor-hub\"},\"schema_version\":\"0.1\",\"severity\":\"INFO\"},{\"data\":{\"category\":\"http\",\"message\":\"two\"},\"event_id\":\"01900000-0000-7000-8000-000000000002\",\"event_type\":\"log.entry.recorded\",\"occurred_at\":\"2026-10-28T10:00:00.123456Z\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-10-28T10:00:00.123456Z\",\"resource\":{\"instance_id\":\"hub-01\",\"service_name\":\"sensor-hub\"},\"schema_version\":\"0.1\",\"severity\":\"INFO\"}],\"schema_version\":\"0.1\"}"
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "status": 200
        }
      ],
      "expected_recorded": {
        "requests": 1,
        "events": 2,
        "invalid": []
      }
    },
